This directory is EMPTY in the repository and populated at deploy time.

deploy.sh rsyncs readme/*.md in here, because the Docker build context is dashboard/
and the Markdown lives at the repo root -- the same reason analysis/epochs.py is copied
in. dashboard/docpage.py renders whatever lands here as the /how/* pages.

It is tracked (via this file) only so `COPY docs/ /app/docs/` in the Dockerfile does not
fail on a build from a clean checkout. The .md files themselves are gitignored: they
would be a second copy of readme/, which is the exact drift this whole arrangement
exists to prevent.

Running locally, this stays empty and docpage.py falls back to ../readme/ directly.
